# Context First

Before planning or implementing any change, read the relevant files under `.specs/codebase/` and `.specs/project/`:

| Change type | Read |
| ----- | ----- |
| General code | `CONVENTIONS.md`, `STRUCTURE.md` |
| Scanner modules (git, complexity, scoring, scan-result, config, report) | `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CONCERNS.md`, `INTEGRATIONS.md` |
| Progress / milestones | `ROADMAP.md`, `.specs/features/` |
| Decisions / deferred / blockers | `STATE.md` |
| Tests | `TESTING.md` |
| Architecture / stack | `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `STACK.md` |
| External integrations | `INTEGRATIONS.md` |
| Fragile areas | `CONCERNS.md` |
| JSON contract | `schemas/`, `TESTING.md` § contract |
| Doc ownership / where content goes | `DOC-OWNERSHIP.md` |
| Agent index / policy pointers | `AGENTS.md` |
| Exit codes | `docs/cli-reference.md` § Exit codes |

## Living documentation

Every significant change (new scanner modules, domain types, CLI flags) must be reflected in the corresponding `.specs/codebase/` files. Feature complete → update [ROADMAP.md](../../.specs/project/ROADMAP.md) per [roadmap-sync.md](../skills/vitals-common/references/roadmap-sync.md).

**Where content goes:** [DOC-OWNERSHIP.md](../../.specs/codebase/DOC-OWNERSHIP.md). When editing a living doc, follow its glob-scoped `*-sot.mdc` rule (and `docs-sot.mdc` for `docs/**`).

## YAGNI

See [coding-guidelines](../skills/coding-guidelines/SKILL.md) (and [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) for the pointer index).
